tps://www.zazastudio.fi/","ph":"+358408351823","wifi":1},{"n":"University Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":60.169575,"lo":24.939536,"d":1365,"h":"08:00-24:00","w":"https://www.yliopistonapteekki.fi/","ph":"+358 300 20200","wp":"fi:Yliopiston Apteekki"},{"n":"St. Henry's Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.1592,"lo":24.9544,"d":94,"ds":"St. Henry's Cathedral is a Catholic cathedral in Helsinki, Finland, dedicated in honor of Bishop Henrik, a 12th-century Bishop of Turku. It is the cathedral church of the Diocese of Helsinki.","wpu":"St. Henry's Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Pyh%C3%A4n_Henrikin_kirkko.jpg/960px-Pyh%C3%A4n_Henrikin_kirkko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Olympia Terminal","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.161111,"lo":24.958056,"d":209,"ds":"The Olympia Terminal (Finnish: Olympiaterminaali, Swedish: Olympiaterminalen) is a dock in the South Harbour of Helsinki, Finland. It was designed by the Hytönen-Luukkonen architects bureau and opened for the 1952 Summer Olympics. Today, the terminal has a regular connection to Stockholm, acting as Silja Line's Helsinki terminal.","wpu":"Olympia Terminal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Olympiaterminaali_IMG_0746.jpg/960px-Olympiaterminaali_IMG_0746.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kaivohuone","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.157539,"lo":24.955919,"d":278,"ds":"Kaivohuone (also abbreviated as Kaivo) is a restaurant in Helsinki, Finland. It is located in the middle of Kaivopuisto Park on the Iso Puistotie street, about one and a half kilometers south of the Market Square. The restaurant features a large outdoor terrace, and in the summer, popular nightclubs performing by top artists are organized in the restaurant, which are especially popular on Wednesdays and Saturdays.","wpu":"Kaivohuone","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Kaivohuone_%2876438%29.jpg/960px-Kaivohuone_%2876438%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mannerheim Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.158861,"lo":24.960444,"d":326,"ds":"The Mannerheim Museum is located in Helsinki, Finland. It is dedicated to preserving and displaying items related to the life and times of Marshal C. G. E. Mannerheim, a Finnish statesman and military officer. The Mannerheim Museum is located on top of a hill in a prestigious residential area next to the Kaivopuisto park in Helsinki.","wpu":"Mannerheim Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Mannerheiminmuseo.jpg/960px-Mannerheiminmuseo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ursa Observatory","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.155472,"lo":24.955417,"d":503,"ds":"The Ursa Observatory (Finnish: Ursan tähtitorni, Swedish: Ursas observatorium) is an astronomical observatory located in the Kaivopuisto park in Helsinki, Finland. The Ursa Astronomical Association observatory, designed by architect Martti Välikangas (1893–1973), was completed in 1926.","wpu":"Ursa Observatory","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Ursan_torni.jpg/960px-Ursan_torni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Museum of Finnish Architecture","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.163056,"lo":24.9475,"d":536,"ds":"The Museum of Finnish Architecture (Finnish: Suomen arkkitehtuurimuseo, Swedish: Finlands arkitekturmuseum) is an architectural museum in Helsinki, Finland. Established in 1956, it is the second oldest museum of its kind (after the Shchusev Museum of Architecture in Moscow) devoted specifically to architecture.","wpu":"Museum of Finnish Architecture","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Kasarmikatu_24_Helsinki.jpg/960px-Kasarmikatu_24_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"South Harbour, Helsinki","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.164722,"lo":24.958333,"d":556,"ds":"South Harbour (Finnish: Eteläsatama, Swedish: Södra hamnen) is a bay and harbour area immediately next to the centre of the city of Helsinki, Finland. 4.7 million passengers in liner traffic and about 37,000 international cruise passengers travel through it every year. Also over million tonnes of unitized cargo passes through the South Harbour.","wpu":"South Harbour, Helsinki","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/South_Harbour_from_air.jpg/960px-South_Harbour_from_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Katajanokka Terminal","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.166389,"lo":24.961667,"d":800,"ds":"Katajanokka Terminal (Finnish: Katajanokan terminaali, Swedish: Skatuddens terminal) is a ferry terminal located in Katajanokka, in the Southern Harbor of Helsinki, Finland. The shipping company Viking Line operates scheduled services from the terminal to Stockholm and Tallinn. The terminal building was originally a customs warehouse, the harbour building K8.","wpu":"Katajanokka Terminal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Katajanokka_ferry_terminal_%28Helsinki%2C_Finland%29_Jun_6%2C_2026.jpg/960px-Katajanokka_ferry_terminal_%28Helsinki%2C_Finland%29_Jun_6%2C_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cholera Basin","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.167222,"lo":24.952917,"d":811,"ds":"The Cholera basin (Finnish: Kolera-allas, Swedish: Kolerabassängen) is the established name for the western harbour basin in front of the Market Square in Helsinki, Finland.","wpu":"Cholera Basin","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Helsinki_Kolera-allas_2007.jpg/960px-Helsinki_Kolera-allas_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Keisarinnankivi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.167639,"lo":24.954444,"d":849,"ds":"Keisarinnankivi (Finnish for \"the stone of the empress\") is a monument located at the Market Square in Kaartinkaupunki in central Helsinki, Finland. The monument, designed by Carl Ludvig Engel, is the oldest public monument in Helsinki.","wpu":"Keisarinnankivi","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Keisarinnankivihelsinginkauppatorilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Havis Amanda","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.1675,"lo":24.951389,"d":857,"ds":"Havis Amanda is a fountain and a statue in Helsinki, Finland by the sculptor Ville Vallgren (1855–1940). The work was modelled in 1906 in Paris, and erected at its present location at the Market Square in Kaartinkaupunki in 1908. Today it is recognized as one of the most important and beloved pieces of art in Helsinki.","wpu":"Havis Amanda","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/%22Havis_Amanda%22%2C_la_statue_de_la_fontaine_de_Vallgren_%28Helsinki%29_%282744386193%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Norrmén house","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.167778,"lo":24.958611,"d":887,"ds":"The Norrmén house, also known as the Norrmén castle and palace, was a red brick residential house representing the neo-renaissance architecture, situated for 63 years in Katajanokka, Helsinki, Finland, opposite the Uspenski Cathedral. It was designed by architect Theodor Höijer for the chairman of the Helsinki city council, Alfred Norrmén, who ordered the building plans from Höijer in 1896.","wpu":"Norrmén house","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Uspenskin_katedraali_ja_Norrm%C3%A9nin_talo_1959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Mikael Agricola Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.1583,"lo":24.9389,"d":910,"ds":"Mikael Agricola Church (Finnish: Mikael Agricolan kirkko, Swedish: Mikael Agricola kyrka) is a Lutheran church located in the Punavuori district of Helsinki, Finland. It was designed by Lars Sonck and built between 1933 and 1935. The church was inaugurated on 14 April 1935.","wpu":"Mikael Agricola Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Helsinki_Mikael_Agricola_church.jpg/960px-Helsinki_Mikael_Agricola_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Esplanadi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.1675,"lo":24.947778,"d":924,"ds":"Esplanadi (Swedish: Esplanaden), colloquially known as Espa, is an esplanade and urban park in downtown Helsinki, Finland, situated between the Erottaja square and the Market Square. It is bordered on its northern and southern sides by the Pohjoisesplanadi (Norra Esplanaden, North Esplanadi) and Eteläesplanadi (Södra Esplanaden, South Esplanadi) streets, respectively. Aleksanterinkatu runs parallel to Esplanadi.","wpu":"Esplanadi","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Esplanadin_puisto_2020.jpg/960px-Esplanadin_puisto_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Wanha Satama","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.165528,"lo":24.967528,"d":926,"ds":"Wanha Satama (Finnish for \"old harbour\") is an exhibition centre in Helsinki, Finland.","wpu":"Wanha Satama","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/11-07-29-helsinki-by-RalfR-007.jpg/960px-11-07-29-helsinki-by-RalfR-007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Uspenski Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.168333,"lo":24.96,"d":967,"ds":"Uspenski Cathedral (Finnish: Uspenskin katedraali, Swedish: Uspenskijkatedralen) is a Greek Orthodox or Eastern Orthodox cathedral in Helsinki, Finland, and main cathedral of the Orthodox Church of Finland, dedicated to the Dormition of the Theotokos (the Virgin Mary). Its name comes from the Old Church Slavonic word uspenie, which denotes the Dormition. It is the largest Orthodox church in Northern Europe.","wpu":"Uspenski Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Catedral_Uspenski%2C_Helsinki%2C_Finlandia%2C_2012-08-14%2C_DD_03.JPG/960px-Catedral_Uspenski%2C_Helsinki%2C_Finlandia%2C_2012-08-14%2C_DD_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Erottaja","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.166667,"lo":24.943333,"d":982,"ds":"Erottaja (Finnish: [ˈerotːɑjɑ]; lit. 'the separator'), Swedish: Skillnaden; Swedish: [ˈʃil.naːden]; lit. 'the difference'), is a public square near the centre of Helsinki, Finland. Erottaja square has been selected as the official geographic \"zero point\" of Helsinki. Distances to all other cities in Finland are measured starting from here.","wpu":"Erottaja","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Erottajankatu_from_Erottaja_square_in_Helsinki%2C_Finland%2C_2021_June.jpg/960px-Erottajankatu_from_Erottaja_square_in_Helsinki%2C_Finland%2C_2021_June.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Eino Leino (statue)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.16757,"lo":24.945229,"d":1000,"ds":"The Eino Leino is a statue of Eino Leino (1878–1926) sculpted by Lauri Leppänen in the Esplanadi Park in Helsinki, Finland. It is located in the northeast corner of Teatteriesplanadi, close to the intersection of the Pohjoisesplanadi and Mikonkatu streets. The statue was unveiled on September 26, 1953, the 63rd anniversary of Leino's publication of his first poem in Hämeen Sanomat.","wpu":"Eino Leino (statue)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Eino_Leino_in_the_park.jpg/960px-Eino_Leino_in_the_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Helsinki, until about 1930 known in English by its Swedish name of Helsingfors, is the capital and most populous city in Finland. It is on the shore of the Gulf of Finland and is the seat of southern Finland's Uusimaa region. About 694,000 people live in the municipality, with 1.3 million in the capital region and 1.6 million in the metropolitan area.","wpu":"Helsinki","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Suomenlinna_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Suomenlinna_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}